       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is double the maximum daily dose. No standard indication supports it, and it adds risk without added benefit. Analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below this dose, so the main effect would be more risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical rationale, so I can't treat this as an intentional exception.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the usual maximum, please talk to pharmacy or the attending before the order goes in. If the goal is better pain control, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a standard dose."
